-- Terrain for the travel path (Path.lua): where you can walk, worked out from the game's own terrain
-- tiles by tools/terrain.py. Squares of 8.3333 yards. Rows run from south to north, columns from east
-- to west. A square is kind * 4 + (1 if you can walk on to the square north of it) + (2 if you can
-- walk on to the square west of it); kinds: 0 easy ground, 1 tight or sloping ground (beside or partly
-- on ground too steep to walk, or sloping over 25 degrees), 2 water, 3 a steep climb (over 40 degrees
-- on average: it can be walked but nobody would choose to); 16 = nothing to stand on (too steep, lava,
-- or off the map).
-- Each character is a run of equal squares. Symbols 35..126 without the backslash, in this order:
--   11:20 16:20 3:14 7:5 15:6 0:2 1:2 2:2 4:2 5:2 6:2 8:2 9:2 10:2 12:2 13:2 14:2   (value:longest run)
-- Built only from a complete set of tiles: tools/terrain.py checks them against the game's own tile index.
-- Stormwind (continent 0): the squares its models touch, and one ring round them, were built again from the
-- city's own models (the collision of its WMO files, exported from the game) by tools/city_build.py.
-- Dalaran (continent 0, the city in Alterac): the squares its models touch, and one ring round them, were built
-- again from the city's own models (tools/city_build.py), and roads under the city were cut there.
-- Zephras Isle (continent 2991): squares its models change were built again, tile by tile, by tools/zeph_build.py:
-- the M2s (rocks, trees, logs, ruins) and the WMOs (buildings, bridges, cave mouths), from the collision the
-- model files carry (exported from the game). A piece lying under the ground (a cave dug under a hill, and
-- what is in it) is left out. Where a WMO is, the rebuilt square is written as it is; elsewhere the M2s only
-- close squares and borders or make ground costlier, they never open a way. Left out, because with them in
-- ground the island reaches without them would be cut off (one floor per square can't join their rooms):
-- 23 placements of 19200.wmo, 20690.wmo, 20691.wmo, 20693.wmo, 20695.wmo, 20779.wmo, 20780.wmo, 21029.wmo, 21052.wmo, azrclassicalelfruin_burned02.wmo, azrclassicalelfruin_burned04.wmo, azrclassicalelfruin_burned06.wmo, azrclassicalelfruin_burned08.wmo, azrclassicalelfruin_burned10.wmo, azrclassicalelfruin_green03.wmo, kl_skywall_entrance_building_01.wmo, kl_skywall_raid_entrance.wmo.
-- Westfall (continent 0): squares its models change were built again by tools/zone_build.py, the same way as
-- Zephras Isle: the M2s (rocks, trees, logs, fences) and the WMOs (buildings, bridges, docks, cave mouths), from the
-- collision the model files carry. Only the zone's own chunks (and one chunk round them) are written; no model may cut
-- off ground the terrain alone reached (such a pocket keeps its squares as they were). Left out: plants,
-- critters and hand-sized clutter (no collision, or too small for 8.3-yd squares); and 38 WMO placements whose files are not fetched yet: elvendestroyerwreckback.wmo, elvendestroyerwreckfront.wmo, elwynnlionbridge.wmo, greatwall_gate.wmo, greatwall_tower_01.wmo, guardtower.wmo, moonbrook_blacksmith.wmo, moonbrook_human_farm.wmo, moonbrook_humantwostory.wmo, moonbrook_inn.wmo, moonbrook_townhall_nowall.wmo, shipwreck_b.wmo, silo.wmo, westfall_barn.wmo, westfall_human_farm.wmo, westfall_humantwostory.wmo, westfall_lumbermill.wmo, westfall_magetower.wmo, westfall_stable.wmo, westfallfarmhouseburnt.wmo, westfallgrainsilo01.wmo; and, because with them in ground the zone reaches without them would be cut off, 1 placements of az_deadmines_a.wmo.
-- Darkshore (continent 1): squares its models change were built again by tools/zone_build.py, the same way as
-- Zephras Isle: the M2s (rocks, trees, logs, fences) and the WMOs (buildings, bridges, docks, cave mouths), from the
-- collision the model files carry. Only the zone's own chunks (and one chunk round them) are written; no model may cut
-- off ground the terrain alone reached (such a pocket keeps its squares as they were). Left out: plants,
-- critters and hand-sized clutter (no collision, or too small for 8.3-yd squares); and 56 WMO placements whose files are not fetched yet: azrclassicalelfruin02.wmo, azrclassicalelfruin04.wmo, azrclassicalelfruin05.wmo, azrclassicalelfruin08.wmo, azrclassicalelfruin10.wmo, blackfathom.wmo, darkshorebridge01.wmo, darkshorebridge02.wmo, darkshorebridge03.wmo, desolacebridge01.wmo, dsexcavationplatform.wmo, dsexcavationrailin.wmo, dsnightelf2story.wmo, dsnightelfhunterslodge.wmo, dsnightelfinn.wmo, dsnightelfmoonwellornate.wmo, dsnightelfsmallhouse.wmo, elvendestroyerwreckback.wmo, elvendestroyerwreckfront.wmo, giantseaturtle01.wmo, giantseaturtle02.wmo, ladder.wmo, nightelfmoonwelldefiled.wmo, old_blackfathom_facade.wmo, redridge_magetower.wmo, shipwreck_a.wmo, shipwreck_b.wmo, troll_hotel01.wmo, trollhutsmall01.wmo, trollshop01.wmo, trollshoppingmall01.wmo, wreckedbuildinghcorner02.wmo.
-- Trees (continents 0 and 1): squares the trees change (their trunks' and roots' collision, from the model files)
-- were built again by tools/tree_build.py, close-only (a tree may close a square or a border or make it costlier,
-- never open a way, nor cut off ground the terrain alone reached), outside the areas built from their own models.
-- Docks (continents 0 and 1): squares on and beside the docks, piers and boardwalks (and Booty Bay's town model)
-- were built again with those models' collision by tools/dock_build.py, outside the areas built from their own models.
